# 01 - UTM Setup and VM Creation

## Objective

Install UTM on macOS and create the virtual machine infrastructure for a SOC L1 homelab.

## Prerequisites

- macOS with Apple Silicon (M1 or newer)
- UTM downloaded from utm.app
- External 1T hard drive with a 200GB partition
- Ubuntu Server ARM64 ISO

## UTM Installation

1. Download UTM from https://mac.getutm.app
2. Move UTM to Applications folder
3. Launch UTM and confirm it opens

## Network Configuration

All VMs use UTM Shared Network mode. This provides:

- Internet access for package downloads
- VM-to-VM communication on the same subnet
- Isolation from the host production network

## VM Storage

Store all VMs on the external drive:

```text
/Volumes/Learning Resources/SOC-L1-Homelab/VMs
```

This preserves internal SSD space for macOS and other applications.

## Lessons Learned

- UTM Virtualize mode is significantly faster than Emulate on Apple Silicon
- Ubuntu Server ARM64 is preferred over Desktop editions for resource efficiency
- Shared Network mode assigns IPs in the 192.168.64.0/24 range

